    "created_at": "2021-12-07T16:05:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-07T16:05:29Z",
    "body": "Are you running the same Volta kernel on Ampere?  Volta tensor core instruction size is 8x8x4 which is no longer natively supported on Ampere.  Ampere uses emulation code to run the old Volta tensor core kernels which is slow.\r\n\r\nAmpere is efficient when running its own large tensor core instruction which is 16x8x16.",
